{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-230124-r4615164","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Mango and Yellow Split Pea Curry","sourcePageId":230124,"sourceRevision":"4615164","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:29:03Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Mango%20and%20Yellow%20Split%20Pea%20Curry&oldid=4615164","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:24.620Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Dal recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes using asafoetida","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using fenugreek leaf","Category:Recipes using galangal","Category:Recipes using garam masala","Category:Recipes using ginger","Category:Recipes using mango","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1ca13780a41563c5df502277107282aa15329fc910c8ac9ab5f47e53a304d70c","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Indian recipes|servings=2|time=25 minutes|difficulty=2}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian]]\n\n'''Mango Dal''' also known as Amchur Dal is a vegetarian dish from Southern [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|India]] which is also popular in the West. The dish is popular amongst vegetarians and persons who wish to limit the amount of meat in their diet.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Pigeon Pea|toor]] [[Cookbook:Dal|dal]]\n* 2 cans [[Cookbook:Mango|mango]] (or fresh mango if available), sliced\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], chopped\n* 1 clove [[Cookbook:Galangal|galangal]] or [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] paste\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|hing]] powder\n* 3 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Garam Masala|garam masala]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Chilli Powder|chilli powder]]\n* 2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Mustard seed|mustard seeds]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Fenugreek|fenugreek]] leaves\n\n==Procedure==\n#Soak dal over night.\n#[[Cookbook:Boiling|Boil]] dal in water. Rinse, drain, and keep in separate container.\n#Boil mango slices in their juice. Add boiled dal and add additional water if required.\n#In a separate pan, [[Cookbook:Sautéing|sauté]] onion, ginger paste, and garlic paste in oil until golden brown.\n#In a separate pan heat ghee, hing, turmeric, garam masala, chilli powder, mustard seeds, and cumin.\n#Add all mixtures together in boiling mango and dal pot.\n#Add fenugreek leaves, and continue boiling.\n#Allow to cool and serve with [[Cookbook:roti|rotis]] or [[Cookbook:naan|naan]] and [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]].\n\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mango]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Dal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fenugreek leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using galangal]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garam masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mango and Yellow Split Pea Curry","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup toor dal","sourceText":"1 cup toor dal","amountText":"1 cup toor dal","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cans mango (or fresh mango if available), sliced","sourceText":"2 cans mango (or fresh mango if available), sliced","amountText":"2 cans mango (or fresh mango if available), sliced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 onion, chopped","sourceText":"1 onion, chopped","amountText":"1 onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 clove galangal or ginger","sourceText":"1 clove galangal or ginger","amountText":"1 clove galangal or ginger","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 teaspoon garlic paste","sourceText":"1 teaspoon garlic paste","amountText":"1 teaspoon garlic paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 teaspoon ghee","sourceText":"1 teaspoon ghee","amountText":"1 teaspoon ghee","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 teaspoon hing powder","sourceText":"1 teaspoon hing powder","amountText":"1 teaspoon hing powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"3 teaspoons turmeric","sourceText":"3 teaspoons turmeric","amountText":"3 teaspoons turmeric","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1 teaspoon garam masala","sourceText":"1 teaspoon garam masala","amountText":"1 teaspoon garam masala","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 teaspoon chilli powder","sourceText":"1 teaspoon chilli powder","amountText":"1 teaspoon chilli powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name"